From 5120a14254719fe7dad329e4a9d4cc5f7b743d12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?A=CC=82nderson=20Q?= <anquadros@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 18:54:32 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] terminal: add toggleable multi-line input editor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a 'toggle: terminal editor' action that opens a 3-row editor docked at the bottom of the terminal for composing input with full editor controls (mouse cursor positioning, selection, multi-row free editing). Enter sends the composed text to the shell; alt-enter inserts a newline; toggling again closes it. Opening is suppressed while a full-screen program (vim, top, ssh, …) owns the terminal.

Addresses the request in discussion #25482 (treat the terminal more like an editor) via a compose-and-send overlay rather than in-shell cursor movement.
---
